0 Kinebrick corrections to the connection table
0 // Snap lines for what neither the LDraw parts nor the LDCad shadow library describe.
0 // Each "0 FILE" block applies to one part, after that part's shadow lines.
0 // Same syntax as the LDCad shadow library, plus extra section shapes (T, a tyre seat; K, a
0 // clutch; B, a bore a part may slide along) and extra line types (!KINEBRICK GEAR: a gear's
0 // tooth count, pitch radius and tooth width, and for bevel gears which side its bevel teeth
0 // face and how far away its pitch cone's tip is; !KINEBRICK SLIDE for parts that click into
0 // set places; !KINEBRICK TRACK for track links, and how far they reach out beyond the line
0 // through their pins; !KINEBRICK GROOVE for grooves a plate slides into edge first).

